{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\n`docs/event-schema.md:256` located `_clear_claimed_session` in `_processors.py`:\n\n```\n_processors.py _clear_claimed_session\n```\n\nThe symbol is defined at `src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py:35` and is not\nimported into, re-exported from, or referenced by `_processors.py`. A reader following\nthe locator opens the wrong module and finds no such symbol.\n\n### State on `origin/main` at `d74d53a5ffd` (re-checked 2026-10-31)\n\nThat line is already corrected. Commit `91429d4531a` (\"Delete reducer _processors\nback-compat re-exports\", ticket `censurable-exotic-snake`) rewrote `:234`, `:249` and\n`:256` to the `reducer/_processors_status.py:<symbol>` form. `:256` now reads\n`` (`reducer/_processors_status.py:_clear_claimed_session`) ``.\n\nThe sweep this ticket asks for still finds one stale locator of the same class.\n`docs/event-schema.md:39` says \"the per-event `process_*` folds are provided through\n`reducer/_processors.py`\". Since `91429d4531a` deleted the back-compat re-exports, 3 of\nthe 18 folds that `reducer/_replay.py` imports are neither defined in nor imported into\n`_processors.py`:\n\n- `process_status` — defined at `reducer/_processors_status.py:86`, imported by\n  `_replay.py:37`.\n- `process_key_event` and `process_signature` — defined at\n  `reducer/_processors_identity.py:44` and `:128`, imported by `_replay.py:36`.\n\nThe other 15 `process_*` folds are defined in `_processors.py` (imported by\n`_replay.py:19-35`).\n\nEvery other module-and-symbol locator in the file was resolved with an AST pass over\nthe named module (definition or import at module top level):\n`_sort.py:prefix_ts` (def L20), `_sort.py:event_sort_key` (def L28),\n`_version.py:KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` (L88), `_version.py:_NON_REPLAY_KNOWN_TYPES` (L47),\n`_version.py:SCHEMA_VERSION` (L41), `_version.py:LEGACY_JIRA_ENV_ID` (L149),\n`_processors_status.py:_fold_close_metadata` (def L67), `:process_status` (def L86),\n`:_fold_claimed_session` (def L21), `:_clear_claimed_session` (def L35),\n`_processors.py:process_create` (def L36), `:_project_legacy_creation_channel`\n(def L134), `:_IMMUTABLE_EDIT_FIELDS` (L303), `:process_edit` (def L306). All resolve.\n\n## How it was found\n\nWhile censusing `_processors.py`'s re-exports for `censurable-exotic-snake`.\n\n## Change\n\nDocumentation only, one file: `docs/event-schema.md`.\n\n1. Rewrite the `:39` sentence so it names the module that defines each fold group:\n   the `process_*` folds live in `reducer/_processors.py`, except `process_status`\n   (`reducer/_processors_status.py`) and `process_key_event` / `process_signature`\n   (`reducer/_processors_identity.py`). Keep the rest of that paragraph unchanged.\n2. Leave `:256` as it is on main (already in the target form).\n\nNo code, test, or other doc file changes. A docs-drift test is not added: the existing\n`docs/` tests do not resolve prose locators, and adding a new locator-resolution gate\nwould be a new mechanism outside this bug's scope.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] **AC1** `grep -cF '_processors.py _clear_claimed_session' docs/event-schema.md`\n      prints 0.\n- [x] **AC2** `grep -cF 'reducer/_processors_status.py:_clear_claimed_session' docs/event-schema.md`\n      prints 1.\n- [x] **AC3** Every locator in `docs/event-schema.md` naming a `reducer/` module and a\n      symbol (or a `process_*` symbol family) resolves: for each, the named module\n      defines or imports the named symbol, verified by an AST read of the module rather\n      than by string match. The check is recorded in a ticket comment listing each\n      locator and its outcome, including the rewritten `:39` sentence.\n- [x] **AC4** `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly\n      `docs/event-schema.md`.\n- [x] **AC5** The Gerrit change for this ticket carries `Verified +1` (CI runs the full\n      `not integration and not external` suite plus lint and typecheck) and\n      `make lint` exits 0 locally.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any change to the reducer modules themselves.\n- Locators in other docs files (`censurable-exotic-snake` already swept the\n  `_processors*` locators under `docs/`)."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793477284912389001,"uuid":"8f0be93e-8733-41ae-ba83-4fd14650bd23"}